<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kōka, Shiga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kōga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kōka is a district and city in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiga-prefecture">Shiga Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, neighbouring the old province of Iga. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> it was governed by a league of local warrior families and, like Iga, was famous for its ninja. Its warriors later served the Tokugawa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koka-shiga.jpg" alt="Kōka, Shiga" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Motokoka · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koka_City_Hall_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
